\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Theoretical input and load-voltage waveforms of the bridge rectifier with a shunt capacitor filter. The dotted curve is the unfiltered output $|v_i|-2V_D$. A diode pair conducts only during the short charging intervals near each crest; between them $C_1$ discharges through $R_1$, which produces the ripple $V_{r(pp)}$. The values of $R_1C_1$ and $2V_D$ are exaggerated for clarity.}}{4}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:theoretical-waveforms}{{4}{4}{Theoretical input and load-voltage waveforms of the bridge rectifier with a shunt capacitor filter. The dotted curve is the unfiltered output $|v_i|-2V_D$. A diode pair conducts only during the short charging intervals near each crest; between them $C_1$ discharges through $R_1$, which produces the ripple $V_{r(pp)}$. The values of $R_1C_1$ and $2V_D$ are exaggerated for clarity}{figure.caption.4}{}}
